now to Idaho in the desperate search for  evidence in the murder of those four  college students there was a vigil held  last night in Boise the state capitol  about 300 miles from the scene of the  crime but there's still no suspect not  even a murder weapon but there is now an  official cause of death for the four  friends who were killed in their home  early Sunday for reasons police still  don't understand  Christina raffini has more from Moscow  Idaho  while authorities in Idaho hunt for a  mass murderer a College Community  remains on edge it was nerve-wracking to  hear them say that we are no longer like  totally safe autopsies are the four  young victims have been completed with  hopes of finding DNA evidence of their  killer on their bodies I was shocked  when I got a call for four homicides  Lata County coroner Kathy Mabbitt  declared the victim's manner of death  stabbing likely from a large knife she  told us the case is one of the worst  she's seen they were pretty involved in  the community so it yeah it feels very  personal the victims are seniors Madison  mojen and Kaylee Gonzalez friends from  separate sororities who lived together  for several years Ethan Chapin a  freshman and triplet who loved playing  basketball and his girlfriend Zana  kernodle a junior who majored in  marketing her father Jeffrey who lives  in Arizona told our Phoenix affiliate  that Zanna had bruises on her arms  possibly from fighting off her attacker  she's a tough kid whatever she wanted to  do she could do it investigators are  trying to piece together a timeline  using live stream video of mojin and  gonsalves at a food truck before they  headed back to their off-campus house  police revealed they are working with  the two surviving roommates who were  home during the attack but are not  considered suspects University officials  say they've increased campus patrols and  are excusing all absences if they want  to leave and go home now they absolutely  can we're going to support them in doing  so  Nate we spoke to a neighbor who was here  at the time of the incident we asked did  he hear anything and he said you know  what no but this is a college town  There's a fraternity house across the  street It's Not Unusual to hear shouts  and yelling and parties and Loud things  on a Saturday night they didn't realize  anything had happened until the next  morning when they saw the cop cars in  front of the house now the FBI  Behavioral analysis team is also here  helping local law enforcement but we're  waiting for the results of that  toxicology report to see what state the  victims were in when they died  still so many questions Christina thank  you
 

